    "reviews": [
      {
        "name": "places/ChIJOfd6YX3I5zsRwtCk41iQ47Y/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT201UmNYWndSR0ZhYkhkYWMxUmFSbUZMYTFWMFRWRRAB",
        "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": {
          "text": "Irish House has always been a good experience for us. Great food, good music, excellent service. But damn is it getting expensive to eat out now. 6000 for 3 people is not cheap. The restaurant layout is great, inviting and feels like an inviting watering hole for those who love their booze. We were literally the first guests that afternoon and yet service was prompt as is expected at all Irish House outlets. Hats off for maintaining the high standards. You normally see sluggish service in a lightly packed restaurant - a means to have the patrons lingering around to get more customers to walk in. That was not what we experienced here. Service was fast. The fish was excellent and the sweet potato fries is always a must have. But man the cheque at the end felt like a ton of rocks. I can’t recollect the garlic shrimp entree costing 725 bucks plus tax anywhere else. Maybe after this experience I will take a much closer look at the menu whenever I go to another Irish House outlet again. No offence guys, it just was too damn expensive….",
          "languageCode": "en"
        },
        "originalText": {
          "text": "Irish House has always been a good experience for us. Great food, good music, excellent service. But damn is it getting expensive to eat out now. 6000 for 3 people is not cheap. The restaurant layout is great, inviting and feels like an inviting watering hole for those who love their booze. We were literally the first guests that afternoon and yet service was prompt as is expected at all Irish House outlets. Hats off for maintaining the high standards. You normally see sluggish service in a lightly packed restaurant - a means to have the patrons lingering around to get more customers to walk in. That was not what we experienced here. Service was fast. The fish was excellent and the sweet potato fries is always a must have. But man the cheque at the end felt like a ton of rocks. I can’t recollect the garlic shrimp entree costing 725 bucks plus tax anywhere else. Maybe after this experience I will take a much closer look at the menu whenever I go to another Irish House outlet again. No offence guys, it just was too damn expensive….",
          "languageCode": "en"
        },
        "authorAttribution": {
